In 1999, Sundar et al.13 suggested a new model to predict the transition between different flow regimes based on momentum exchange between gas and liquid. This momentum exchange acts principally in the vicinity of the gas core and the liquid film adjacent to the gas core that is subjected to positive acceleration given by the liquid momentum. Meanwhile, the liquid is also subjected to negative acceleration due to gravity. Thus, because of these two inverse forces, the liquid film tends to collapse, which tends to shut off the gas channel. Thus13, reported that the transition from bubbling to jetting appeared when the upward acceleration of the liquid film is zero at the top of the liquid level. Work by Taitel et al.14 was analogical to this report as well. After comparison with their mathematical model and experimental data, the final empirical equation13 for transition was obtained:6\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
